            <ArticleTitle>Fibromyalgia: helping your patient while maintaining your sanity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>743-55, vi</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.pop.2010.07.007</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In caring for the patient with fibromyalgia, the primary care provider benefits from an understanding of fibromyalgia as a distinct entity. Evidence-based diagnostic criteria for fibromyalgia can be used in all individuals who present with multiple site pain, fatigue, and poor sleep. Planning therapy for individuals with fibromyalgia often involves using both pharmacologic and nonpharmacologic treatment in the primary care setting.</AbstractText>
